<title>HUNGARY: Hungary releases detailed April CPI figures.</title>
<headline>Hungary releases detailed April CPI figures.</headline>
<dateline>BUDAPEST 1997-05-12</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hungary's Central Statistical Office (KSH) released detailed April consumer price index (CPI) figures on Monday.</p>
<p>CPI PCT CHANGE IN MAIN PRODUCT GROUPS</p>
<p>				  April 1997		Weight in</p>
<p>				mth/mth   yr/yr	   index (pct)</p>
<p> Food products		1.5     14.9	     28.6</p>
<p>Alcoholic</p>
<p>beverages/</p>
<p>  tobacco products	  1.3     20.7		9.0</p>
<p> Clothing		     3.0     19.5		6.3</p>
<p> Durable consumer goods   0.3	8.0		6.2</p>
<p> Household energy	   0.8     35.2		8.0</p>
<p> Other goods, fuels	 1.4     18.9	     17.0</p>
<p> Services		     1.4     19.1	     24.9</p>
<p> Total			  1.4     18.6	    100.0</p>
<p>NOTE - The CPI was boosted by government measures by 0.1 percent within the total 1.4 percent month-on-month rise in April, the KSH said.</p>
<p>-- Budapest newsroom (36 1) 327 4040</p>
</text>
